			"notes": "# Automated Materials Index\n\nBrowse materials and their uses across installed Minecraft mods.\n\nProvided **AS IS**, without warranty. Support and updates are best effort.\n\nLicense: **MIT**. The original license files, copyright notices, attribution and separate asset terms remain in force.\n\n## Downloads\n\n| Runtime JAR | Loader | Minecraft |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ami-fabric-1.21.1-1.8.7.jar` | Fabric | `~1.21.1` |\n| `ami-forge-1.20.1-1.8.7.jar` | Forge | `[1.20.1, 1.21)` |\n| `ami-neoforge-1.21.1-1.8.7.jar` | NeoForge | `[1.21.1]` |\n\nInstall one matching runtime JAR per mod, with its required dependencies, in `mods/`. Close Minecraft before replacing an existing JAR. Do not install source archives as mods.\n\n## Required dependencies\n\n- **Fabric / ami-fabric-1.21.1-1.8.7.jar**: `fabric-api` *.\n- **Forge / ami-forge-1.20.1-1.8.7.jar**: `forge` [47,).\n- **NeoForge / ami-neoforge-1.21.1-1.8.7.jar**: `neoforge` [21.1.200,).\n\n## Verification and source\n\n- Gradle completed successfully: `build`.\n- This release preparation verified the build and packaged metadata; it does not certify every gameplay path or modpack combination.\n- Published source commit: `dc5f40f661fabf696e552385f6b8e42a99793388`.\n- [Corresponding source at this release](https://github.com/ashleywr/AutomatedMaterialsIndex/tree/ashley-2026.10.25-dc5f40f6). GitHub also provides source ZIP/tar archives below.\n- `SHA256SUMS.txt` records the SHA-256 checksum of every attached runtime JAR."
